(*
MagTagChordNode — proves CHORDING ("hold A, press B") on the MagTag by READING pin
level on a press, rather than by tracking a doubled press/release event stream.

HOW IT WORKS. Each button registers ONE press event (its GPIO number). On any press
the node reads the live level of all four buttons via `gpio level: n` and prints the
held set. Holding A and pressing B reads level 15 == true at the instant B fires, so
the line is held=AB — no per-button flag, no release pin, no second event.

  BUTTON_A 15   BUTTON_B 14   BUTTON_C 12   BUTTON_D 11

WHY THIS REPLACES RELEASE EVENTS (tuvm#84, follows #82). The earlier version of this
node (a6656d3) registered a second logical pin per button — the settled release on
GPIO + 100 — and kept a held-flag it flipped on press and release. That worked, but
doubled the event rate to carry state the node can now simply ASK for when it cares.
`gpio level:` landed in #82 and is proven here and in MagTagLedNode.nsl (gate 2). So
the release-fire branch and OEVM_BUTTON_RELEASE_BASE are gone from src/main.c; the
debounce state machine still watches the release EDGE internally, purely to re-arm.

LEVEL IS PULL, NOT PUSH. A release produces no event now, so the `up` lines the old
node printed are GONE by construction — the node observes state only when a button is
pressed. That is the trade the design chose (2026-07-23-magtag-buttons-leds-design.md,
Deferred / D7): zero mailbox traffic for held-state, at the cost of not seeing a
release until the next press.

TRUSTWORTHY BECAUSE DEBOUNCED. main.c fires a press only on a settled
released -> pressed transition, so the press that triggers the read is real; and the
level read itself honours GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW, so `true` means "down" on this ACTIVE_LOW
board.

expect — hold A, tap B; hold A+C, tap D; then tap B alone:
B down   held=AB
D down   held=ACD
B down   held=B
*)
class MagTagChordNode packageUsing: manifest = (
) (
  heldOf: gpio = (
    | s |
    s:: ''.
    (gpio level: 15) ifTrue: [ s:: s , 'A' ].
    (gpio level: 14) ifTrue: [ s:: s , 'B' ].
    (gpio level: 12) ifTrue: [ s:: s , 'C' ].
    (gpio level: 11) ifTrue: [ s:: s , 'D' ].
    ^ s
  )

  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space gpio aDn bDn cDn dDn |
    space:: platform space.
    gpio:: platform gpio.

    aDn:: space channel: 'btn/a/down'.
    bDn:: space channel: 'btn/b/down'.
    cDn:: space channel: 'btn/c/down'.
    dDn:: space channel: 'btn/d/down'.

    aDn whenever: '' do: [ :m | ('A down   held=' , (self heldOf: gpio)) println ].
    bDn whenever: '' do: [ :m | ('B down   held=' , (self heldOf: gpio)) println ].
    cDn whenever: '' do: [ :m | ('C down   held=' , (self heldOf: gpio)) println ].
    dDn whenever: '' do: [ :m | ('D down   held=' , (self heldOf: gpio)) println ].

    gpio pin: 15 edge: #falling post: 'A' on: aDn.
    gpio pin: 14 edge: #falling post: 'B' on: bDn.
    gpio pin: 12 edge: #falling post: 'C' on: cDn.
    gpio pin: 11 edge: #falling post: 'D' on: dDn.

    [ true ] whileTrue: [ platform pumpEvents. space drain ]
  )
) : (
)
